AB  - Online education continues to evolve at a rapid pace, but today's traditional learning platforms are often insufficiently personalised, interactive, and hard to measure in terms of learning outcomes. In this study, an intelligent interaction system for online learning is designed and implemented, which adopts a flexible framework and adds a multi-level security protection. The system includes functions for learning programme intelligent scheduling, real-time learning progress detection, and appropriate learning content recommendation. The system incorporates a learning habit analysis model and a knowledge network technique for designing personalised learning paths, and is built using a common web framework. Testing has shown that it is stable with many concurrent users and that key features are working well, greatly improving learning effectiveness and resource utilisation. This opens up a new direction for the realisation of more intelligent online education.  © 2025 IEEE.
