TI  - High-Fidelity Comparative Text Synthesis from Multi-Format Financial Data: A Cascaded Extraction Pipeline Driven by Deep OCR and a Transformer NLP Model with RAG for Semantic Fact Generation
PY  - 2026
T2  - International Conference on Artificial Intelligence, Computer, Data Sciences, and Applications, ACDSA 2026
DO  - 10.1109/ACDSA67686.2026.11467784
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105037653897?origin=resultslist
AB  - In this paper, a novel high-fidelity cascaded extraction and generation framework designed to transform heterogeneous corporate financial data into accurate, verifiable, and interpretable textual narratives. The proposed pipeline integrates Deep Optical Character Recognition (OCR), Transformer-based Natural Language Processing (NLP), and Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) to unify information across multi-format financial disclosures such as PDFs, XBRL, CSV etc. Unlike prior systems that decouple extraction and narrative synthesis, the architecture fuses these processes within a single cascaded pipeline: (1) multi-format ingestion and OCRdriven parsing, (2) data normalization and schema alignment, (3) semantic context retrieval using BERT/MiniLM embeddings indexed with FAISS, and factual text synthesis through a T5-Base transformer enhanced with numeric validation. The pipeline achieves semantic grounding between numeric and textual elements, ensuring factual integrity during narrative generation. To enhance interpretability, an interactive web application was developed, providing dynamic visual analytics such as Profit Margin, Debt-to-Equity, Return on Assets (ROA), Assets vs. Liabilities, Year-over-Year (YoY) Growth, Correlation Matrix, and Company Comparison. Each visualization links back to source data for analysis. Also, its seamless integration of multimodal data extraction, semantic retrieval, and visualization within a unified architecture, establishing a reproducible foundation for high-fidelity financial analytics. © 2026 IEEE.
