TI  - Azzurra: A Proof-of-Concept Avatar to Smoothly Interact with the Encyclopedia of Italian Cuisine
PY  - 2025
T2  - IEEE International Conference on Data Mining Workshops, ICDMW
SP  - 623
EP  - 632
DO  - 10.1109/ICDMW69685.2025.00076
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105035381009?origin=resultslist
AB  - Preserving cultural culinary heritage requires innovative approaches that balance scientific accuracy and public accessibility. This work presents Azzurra, a conversational digital avatar that democratizes access to traditional Italian culinary knowledge through multimodal artificial intelligence. Azzurra integrates photorealistic neural rendering, large language models, and a knowledge base validated by the Encyclopedia of Italian Cuisine (ECI) developed by CREA - Food and Nutrition Research Centre. The system implements a knowledge-grounded conversational AI paradigm that combines anthropomorphic visual representation and domain-specific natural language understanding to deliver scientifically accurate and engaging dialogue experiences. The hybrid architecture uses out-of-the-box (OOB) technologies (HeyGen, ChatGPT) orchestrated through custom layers that anchor responses to nutritional and cultural data. The system supports web and holographic deployments, with the latter demonstrating engagement during validation at the 'Agricoltura È' event in Rome. Innovations include: structured prompt engineering with data, multi-level conversational guardrails for the nutritional domain, scalable multimodal architecture, and proven effectiveness in making complex nutritional information accessible. Qualitative validation reveals strong user engagement and perceived scientific reliability. The work outlines future evolutions to overcome OOB limitations through semantic knowledge graphs, advanced RAG, intelligent personalization, innovative interaction modes, and temporal mining. Azzurra demonstrates the feasibility of conversational AI for cultural preservation, establishing a methodological framework for UNESCO intangible heritage and contributing to 'active preservation' through interaction. © 2025 IEEE.
