AB  - With the rapid development of online education, English learning platforms face challenges in personalized recommendation. By constructing an intelligent recommendation model based on data mining algorithms, this study adopts a hierarchical microservice architecture that integrates collaborative filtering, content-based recommendation, and deep learning algorithms. The system performs multi-dimensional feature extraction on 100,000 user data points and implements recommendation algorithm fusion using weighted hybrid strategies, achieving an accuracy rate of 72.8%. Combined with knowledge graphs and reinforcement learning algorithms for learning path planning, learning efficiency is improved by 18.6%. Experimental validation demonstrates that this model outperforms traditional methods in both recommendation accuracy and learning effectiveness, providing technical support for the intelligent development of English learning platforms. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
