AB  - This paper presents a comprehensive review of Artificial Intelligence (AI) applications in Model-Driven Architecture (MDA), a structured software engineering approach that organizes system development through layered models: the Computation-Independent Model (CIM), Platform-Independent Model (PIM), and Platform-Specific Model (PSM). AI has become a transformative force across all MDA stages, from requirements interpretation to automated code generation. Our study systematically analyzes 56 primary studies (2018-2025) from five major scientific databases using rigorous inclusion and exclusion criteria. We examine how AI techniques enhance key MDA processes, including model transformation, semantic consistency, and software synthesis. The review identifies critical challenges such as modeling ambiguity, reliability concerns in AI-generated outputs, and generalizability limitations. To address these challenges, we propose a novel Context-Aware MDA (CA-MDA) framework enhanced by Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), which improves accuracy and traceability while mitigating common AI risks. The findings provide a structuredoverview of AI-enhanced MDA, highlight current trends, and offer practical insights for researchers and practitioners in model-driven software engineering. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2027.
