TI  - HyMed: An Event-Driven Multi-agent Framework for Smart Hospitals
PY  - 2027
T2  - Lecture Notes in Computer Science
VL  - 16670 LNCS
SP  - 393
EP  - 402
DO  - 10.1007/978-981-92-3495-0_33
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105046242687?origin=resultslist
AB  - Multimodal medical artificial intelligence is transitioning from proof-of-concept to large-scale clinical deployment, yet existing systems remain hindered by information silos, low AI trustworthiness, and poor reusability. To address these challenges, we propose HyMed (Hybrid Medical Intelligent Agent Collaboration Framework), a hospital-wide intelligent framework built on three tightly integrated innovations. It adopts a four-terminal asynchronous decoupled collaboration mechanism driven by an event bus, enabling dynamic cross-role coordination among doctors, nurses, patients, and administrators. The framework also provides a bidirectional trustworthy AI mechanism that combines Retrieval-Augmented Generation with Evidence Chains (RAG-E) and image-text consistency verification to suppress AI hallucinations. In addition, it equips a Medical Agent Toolkit (MATK) with a configurable prompt framework to support high-reusability clinical function development. Experimental validation demonstrates that RAG-E reduces the hallucination rate from 6.37% to 1.92%, improves semantic consistency scores from 0.817 to 0.900, and achieves 98% evidence traceability. Architectural experiments confirm a 22.7% reduction in fault recovery time and scalable horizontal expansion with negligible performance impact. HyMed provides a replicable and standards-aligned technical foundation for the next generation of smart hospitals. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Singapore Pte Ltd. 2027.
