AB  - An increasing demand for personalised learning is seen in the current educational environment, and individual differences among learners are not effectively addressed by traditional teaching models. The paper’s focus is on the design and implementation of a personalised learning system based on a microservice architecture. This system integrates multi-dimensional user profiling, hybrid recommendation algorithms and adaptive learning path generation technology in an innovative way. Adopting a layered design, the system achieves core functions such as data collection, intelligent recommendation, learning analysis and interactive interfaces. The experiments show that the system makes learning much more efficient and helps students to master knowledge, closing the gap between students with different starting points. It also exhibits excellent scalability and adaptability. The study’s results offer fresh, useful examples for the growth and usage of smart education tech. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
